    "start_char": 0,
    "end_char": 785,
    "text": "In a competitive market, buyers create demand and sellers create supply. The market price coordinates their plans. When the price rises, buyers usually demand a smaller quantity, while sellers usually supply a larger quantity. When the price falls, those responses reverse.\n\nIf quantity demanded exceeds quantity supplied, a shortage puts upward pressure on price. The higher price decreases quantity demanded and increases quantity supplied until the shortage narrows. If quantity supplied exceeds quantity demanded, a surplus puts downward pressure on price.\n\nPrice elasticity measures how strongly quantity responds to a price change. When demand is less elastic, a similar reduction in supply can cause a larger price increase because buyers reduce their quantity demanded by less.",
